# The flicker maps are the artefact; its results file holds only the adapter.
results-real-flicker.json
# And the same for the motion pictures, which are the evidence rather than the
# numbers. results-motion.json IS committed, because a research page reads it
# and a checkout without it cannot build the site.
results-motion-pictures.json
# And a run of one measurement out of the motion group, which writes its own
# file that no page reads. The committed one is results-motion.json, written by
# `run.mjs motion`, and a stray half of it beside that is how a reader ends up
# looking at the wrong numbers.
results-attribution.json
